# All text files: detect line ending automatically AND store as LF
# in the working tree on every platform. biome.json's formatter sets
# `"lineEnding": "lf"` and treats CRLF as a format violation; without
# this rule, Windows clones with `core.autocrlf=true` (Git for Windows
# default) end up with CRLF in the working tree and biome ci fails on
# the Windows GitHub Actions runner with "File content differs from
# formatting output" on every source file.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Belt-and-braces explicit rules for files that ABSOLUTELY must be LF
# regardless of the catch-all above (in case it's ever weakened or
# someone overrides it locally):

# Files that get baked into Linux container images. A CRLF in the
# shebang (#!/bin/sh\r\n) makes the kernel try to exec `/bin/sh\r`
# and fail with "no such file or directory".
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf

# pnpm-lock.yaml: LF keeps the file hash stable across platforms
# (pnpm computes integrity hashes on the file contents).
pnpm-lock.yaml text eol=lf

# Common binary file types: don't try to detect or convert.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.tar binary
